# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values from your Supabase
# project settings (Project Settings -> API). Never commit .env.local.
#
# Only the anon (public) key belongs here. The service role key must never be
# placed in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or used anywhere in frontend code.

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS -- used solely for public, read-only aggregate
# reads that RLS has no anon-readable path for (landing page stats, and
# checking whether a posting company's account is ACTIVE for the featured
# opportunities section). See src/lib/supabase/admin.ts. Without this set,
# both degrade gracefully rather than crash: the stats section hides itself,
# and featured opportunities renders its normal empty state (since no
# company can be confirmed ACTIVE without this key).
#
# Also required (only when passing --commit) by scripts/seed-demo-accounts.ts,
# to call the Auth admin API and to bypass RLS for the profile-table inserts.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. Shared login password for every account scripts/seed-demo-accounts.ts
# creates. Defaults to a fixed demo password (see the script) if unset.
# SEED_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD=

# LINE notification linking (review #8). Server-only -- never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# LINE Login is used purely to obtain a verified line_user_id for an already
# signed-in Engineer Match session; it is never a Supabase Auth sign-in
# method (see src/app/auth/line/callback/route.ts). See LINE Developers
# Console: create a Provider with one LINE Login channel (callback URL
# https://<domain>/auth/line/callback) and one Messaging API channel, linked
# together so "Add friend option" is available during LINE Login consent.
# LINE_LOGIN_CHANNEL_ID=
# LINE_LOGIN_CHANNEL_SECRET=

# Messaging API channel (the linked official account that actually sends
# notification pushes). Webhook URL: https://<domain>/api/line/webhook.
# LINE_MESSAGING_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# LINE_MESSAGING_CHANNEL_SECRET=

# Shared secret between the (future) notifications dispatch trigger --
# migration 079, not yet written, held until pg_net is enabled on the remote
# project -- and src/app/api/line/dispatch/route.ts. Not used by anything
# built so far in this phase; safe to leave unset until 079 exists.
# LINE_DISPATCH_SHARED_SECRET=

# Public "add friend" URL for the linked Messaging API official account
# (LINE Developers Console -> Messaging API channel -> QR code / Bot basic
# ID). Shown in Engineer Settings when a linked user hasn't added the OA as
# a friend yet. Not a secret -- safe as NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINE_OA_ADD_FRIEND_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MINE_APP_URL=https://mine-omega-one.vercel.app

